```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: red
REAL_USE_CASE: Multi-tenant agentic LLM serving fleets where near-identical tool-schema/boilerplate spans are embedded at different offsets across system prompts, causing exact-prefix block hashing (vLLM APC, RadixAttention) to miss sharing opportunities.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Microbenchmark-only. Token-level CDC finds 4–7% offset-shifted duplicate blocks beyond exact-prefix, but position-aware (RoPE-correct) reclaim collapses to 0.35–1.46% across N=16–128 tenants (packet: "position-aware gain collapses to 0.35-1.46% (below the pre-registered threshold)"). The 4–7% upper bound does not survive production RoPE position-dependence, and 0.35–1.46% is below the pre-registered "few %" threshold, yielding no measurable batch-size or preemption reduction.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [RoPE bakes absolute position into K tensors, so offset-shifted identical spans are not raw-KV identical without a re-rotation transform R(delta); CDC variable-length chunks misalign with 16-token KV-block granularity; cheap re-rope must beat recompute cost, which is unproven; prior-art sweep owed for LMCache, KVQuant, CacheBlend prefix-independent KV reuse that directly targets RoPE re-anchoring; production paged kernels already optimize prefix sharing; reclaimed memory <1.5% does not translate to operational throughput wins]
RATIONALE: Packet EXP-0009 reports "position-dependence destroys ~80–95% of that gain" and "VERDICT: NEGATIVE. At the raw-KV level, CDC dedup does NOT meaningfully beat exact-prefix sharing for offset-shifted agent boilerplate, because position-dependence (RoPE) means offset-shifted identical token spans are NOT identical KV tensors." Control with aligned schemas shows exact-prefix already reclaims 20.2%, confirming the claim's shifted regime is the only relevant case, where position-aware CDC beyond-prefix is ≤1.46%. The negative result is actionable: it directs follow-up to measure whether a cheap R(delta) re-rotation (CacheBlend-adjacent) can recover the 4–7% token-level ceiling, otherwise the mechanism is not operationally viable.
```
